    {
      "name": "D13",
      "label": "GPIO13 (Led active high)",
      "codeName": "D13",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_high"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED / D13 — onboard plain red status LED, active-high. Confirmed via Zephyr's adafruit_metro_rp2040.dts leds node (gpios = <&gpio0 13 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>) and Adafruit's own learn.adafruit.com pinouts guide (\"This red LED on 13 is user controllable for blinky needs\"). digital_input dropped to match this repo's established led_high precedent for dedicated onboard LED pins (rpipico, adafruit_feather_scorpio); pwm_output kept since arduino-pico's analogWrite() works on any RP2040 GPIO, enabling brightness dimming. No SPI/Wire/Serial alias exists on this GPIO in this board's pins_arduino.h, so no bus-alias-contamination fix was needed (contrast adafruit_feather_scorpio)."
    },
    {
      "name": "D14",
      "label": "GPIO14 (Led Neopixel)",
      "codeName": "D14",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "led_neopixel"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_NEOPIXEL — onboard single status NeoPixel (WS2812), output-only data line. Confirmed via Adafruit's own learn.adafruit.com pinouts and neopixel-led guides (\"This addressable RGB NeoPixel LED is both a status LED and user controllable on 14\"; single built-in NeoPixel, not a chain), Zephyr's adafruit_metro_rp2040.dts ws2812 node (gpios = <&gpio0 14 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>, chain-length = <1>), and CircuitPython mpconfigboard.h (MICROPY_HW_NEOPIXEL -> pin_GPIO14). No SPI/Wire/Serial alias exists on this GPIO in this board's pins_arduino.h."
    },
